y JQL summary~ hit, and JQL text search is fuzzy, so in shared REB it could delete an unrelated issue (the Python backstop already re-checks the exact prefix). Follow-up commit 8fa210ad340 makes the step delete only hits whose summary contains the run prefix verbatim, with a test pinning it; exercised for real with a non-matching prefix and against a fuzzy/exact sample. make verify running.","timestamp":1794532855657005001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Live run evidence (AC4): Live External Integration https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/43343447995 on main at 9da38e2a526, conclusion success. Job \"jira Cloud coordinator mutation probe (bounded, self-cleaning, real Cloud)\" (job 131617036462, run label rebar-id:cloudprobe-43343447995) passed 4 tests in 788 s, including the 2 new ones: test_cloud_fix_versions.py::test_releases_round_trip_on_one_issue PASSED and ::test_missing_version_is_withheld_then_written PASSED.\nVersion search afterwards, 2026-11-12 17:36 PST: GET /rest/api/3/project/REB/version?query=cloudprobe-43343447995 returned total 0, no versions.\ntests/external/live_jira_cloud_s3 is unchanged by this work (git diff on main shows no change under it).","timestamp":1794533809483688001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Completion evidence:\n- Gerrit 3386 merged as 9da38e2a526 (submitted 17:14 PST) and follow-up 3388 merged as 3402817d294 (submitted 18:26 PST), each at LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, 0 unresolved.\n- AC1: tests/external/live_jira_cloud_mutation/test_cloud_fix_versions.py covers scenarios 1-4 with real bootstrap-strict reconcile passes against live REB, no Jira fakes.\n- AC2: run-scoped issue labels and version names; deleted in finally; conftest backstop and the workflow failure/cancel step also sweep run-prefixed versions and issues (exact prefix match in both).\n- AC3: live_jira_cloud_s3 unchanged.\n- AC4: live run 43343447995 passed both new tests; REB version search for cloudprobe-43343447995 returned 0 (comment above).\n- AC5: make verify exit 0 on 305bf97267b (16:05-16:45 PST) and on the follow-up 8fa210ad340 (17:20-17:57 PST).\n- AC6: README lists the scenarios and version cleanup.\n- AC7: per-item writes asserted from the RECON: outbound_update line in the round-trip test, which passed live.","timestamp":1794536813988095001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"HANDOFF STATE 2026-11-12 18:33 PST (session 3d705fec): CLOSED. Gerrit 3386 (9da38e2a526) and follow-up 3388 (3402817d294) merged; live run 43343447995 passed both new tests and left no run-prefixed versions; completion gate passed on the Anthropic API. Worktree removed.","timestamp":1794537233298101001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1794514111016867173,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"989c3d25-1c98-4dd6-b6e8-54a8d31a636f","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"21ec-3e9b-4a27-4775"},{"link_uuid":"dc5dec5e-e98d-40ce-85b2-d1330b97d9fb","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"af08-19c2-87b4-41d3"},{"link_uuid":"7325bd3b-50da-4a88-80d5-87e40e8e5158","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"96b6-e89c-a78e-463e"},{"link_uuid":"32e4d76e-3a90-4006-8694-60b42884170d","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"a15a-6936-2cee-479a"}],"description":"## Problem\n\nFix-version sync (ADR 0124, epic `inferior-seaborgium-aruanas`) is tested only against fakes. Unit tests and the fake-backed `tests/integration/reconciler/test_reconcile_releases_roundtrip.py` are the only automated coverage. Production Jira Cloud was checked live once, by hand (`plucky-jetblack-parrot`, `cognitive-sooty-angelfish`), and no automated test repeats that check.\n\nThe Cloud write and version-read paths (`src/rebar/reconciler/adapters/jira/acli_graph.py` and `src/rebar/reconciler/adapters/jira/acli_rest.py`) have no live regression test. This story is the Cloud counterpart of `ravenous-centric-guppy`, which adds the same coverage to the Jira DC Docker suite.\n\n## Plan\n\nAdd fix-version scenarios to `tests/external/live_jira_cloud_mutation`. That suite is the bounded, self-cleaning write suite that runs against the shared REB project. It runs in the `jira-cloud-mutation-probe` job of `.github/workflows/external-integration.yml`.\n\nDo not put these scenarios in `live_jira_cloud_s3`. That suite is read-only, and its `readonly_jira_guard` must stay intact.\n\nReuse the suite's existing safety model:\n- Every issue created carries the run-scoped `REBAR_PROBE_RUN_LABEL`.\n- Each test deletes the issues it creates in `finally`.\n- The autouse label sweep and the workflow's always-run delete step are the crash backstop.\n\nExtend that model to versions. Every version the test creates gets a unique, run-scoped name (for example `cloudprobe-<run_id>-a`). The owning test deletes it in `finally`. The backstop sweep also removes versions carrying the run prefix.\n\nThe scenarios run real reconcile passes against Jira Cloud:\n\n1. Inbound sync: a run-scoped version is created in REB and set on a throwaway issue's `fixVersions`. It appears in the bound rebar ticket's `releases`.\n2. Outbound add: a release added in rebar for an existing run-scoped version is written to `fixVersions`. Adding a second release keeps the first, so the write is per item.\n3. Outbound remove: a release removed in rebar disappears from `fixVersions`, and the other entries stay.\n4. A missing version is held back: a release naming a run-scoped version that does not exist yet is not written. Instead the ticket gets a BRIDGE_ALERT, and the alert clears once the version is created and a later pass writes it.\n\nBound the blast radius to one throwaway issue per test. Unlike the suite's existing coordinator tests, these run full reconcile passes, so the bound comes from `--filter-local-ids`, which dispatches mutations only for the selected ticket and its bound key.\n\n## Implementation notes (added 2026-11-12, session 3d705fec)\n\n- **Pass cost decides the test shape.** Every reconcile pass fetches all of REB, and `--filter-local-ids` narrows only what is dispatched. One read-only dry-run pass against REB took 136 s (measured 2026-11-12 15:04 PST). The job allows 45 minutes, so the 4 scenarios run in 2 tests with 8 passes in total, not 4 tests with about 14. The longer test runs 5 passes plus search waits (up to 180 s each, 3 waits), about 20 minutes in the worst case, inside the step's per-test `--timeout=1800`:\n  - `test_releases_round_trip_on_one_issue`: bind, then outbound add of version A, outbound add of B (A stays), outbound remove of A (B stays), then inbound: C set on the issue in Jira arrives in `releases`.\n  - `test_missing_version_is_withheld_then_written`: bind, then a release naming a version that does not exist is withheld with a `release-version-missing:<name>` alert, then the version is created and the next pass writes it and resolves the alert.\n  - Each test still touches exactly one throwaway issue.\n- **Binding.** The ticket is created locally (`rebar.create_ticket`) with the run prefix in its title, and is bound by a `bootstrap-strict` pass scoped with `--filter-local-ids <local_id>`. That pass creates one REB issue labelled `rebar-id:<local_id>`, and the test adds the run label right after. Seeding the issue first and labelling it would block the inbound bind, because Jira-only issues carrying a `rebar-id` label are skipped. Until the run label lands, the issue is found by its summary instead: the conftest backstop and the workflow cleanup also delete REB issues whose summary contains the run prefix, and each test's `finally` also deletes by its `rebar-id:<local_id>` label.\n- **Intent and lag.** Outbound adds and removes act only on releases rebar set itself, so releases are set with `rebar.edit_ticket(add_releases=/remove_releases=)`. `fixVersions` reaches the pass through JQL search, so the test waits for search to show the expected versions before each follow-up pass.\n- **Permissions.** Checked 2026-11-12: the CI Jira identity (`vars.JIRA_USER`) has ADMINISTER_PROJECTS on REB (`/rest/api/3/mypermissions`), which version create and delete require, plus EDIT_ISSUES and DELETE_ISSUES.\n- **Per item.** The pass that adds B and the pass that removes A must each log `RECON: outbound_update key=<KEY> ... releases=1` with `fixVersions` absent from `changed`. The issue must also end with the other version still present.\n- **Versions.** Names are `<run prefix>-<label>-<hex>`, where the run prefix is the run label without `rebar-id:`: `cloudprobe-<run_id>` in CI, `cloudprobe-local-<hex>` locally. `run_label()` is fixed once per process, so the test and the local backstop share one prefix (today it changes on every call when the env var is unset). They are created and deleted over REST (`POST /rest/api/3/version`, `DELETE /rest/api/3/version/{id}`) through the `AcliClient` raw REST helpers, and each test deletes its versions in `finally`. The autouse backstop also deletes REB versions whose name starts with the run prefix. The workflow's existing cleanup step does the same with curl, and its tests are extended to cover that.\n- **Files:** a new `test_cloud_fix_versions.py`; version helpers and a version sweep in `_cloud_mutation_support.py`; the backstop in `conftest.py`; the cleanup step in `.github/workflows/external-integration.yml` and its test `tests/unit/test_external_integration_cloud_mutation_workflow.py`; and the suite README, whose \"exactly one plan, no `--filter-local-ids`\" statement is changed to say it holds for the coordinator tests, while the fix-version tests bound themselves with `--filter-local-ids`. `live_jira_cloud_s3` is not touched.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] New tests in `tests/external/live_jira_cloud_mutation/` cover scenarios 1 to 4 above against live Jira Cloud, with real reconcile passes and no fakes on the Jira side.\n- [x] Every version and issue the tests create carries the run label or run-scoped name. Each test deletes them in `finally`, and the conftest sweep and the workflow's always-run cleanup step also remove leftover run-scoped versions.\n- [x] `tests/external/live_jira_cloud_s3` is unchanged, and its read-only guard tests pass.\n- [x] [non-codebase] A `jira-cloud-mutation-probe` run of `external-integration.yml` on a commit containing the new tests passes, with the new tests listed as passed. Afterwards, a REB version search for the run prefix returns no versions. The run URL and that search result are recorded in a comment on this ticket.\n  provenance: environment=GitHub Actions external-integration.yml jira-cloud-mutation-probe job on main, against Jira Cloud project REB; principal=vars.JIRA_USER Jira Cloud account with ADMINISTER_PROJECTS on REB; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — workflow_dispatch run log plus a REB version search for the run prefix\n- [x] `make verify` passes on the change.\n- [x] `tests/external/live_jira_cloud_mutation/README.md` lists the new scenarios and the version cleanup.\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/external/live_jira_cloud_mutation/test_cloud_fix_versions.py","reason":"new fix-version scenarios against live Cloud"},{"path":"tests/external/live_jira_cloud_mutation/_cloud_mutation_support.py","reason":"run-scoped version helpers and version sweep"},{"path":"tests/external/live_jira_cloud_mutation/conftest.py","reason":"backstop also sweeps run-scoped versions"},{"path":"tests/external/live_jira_cloud_mutation/README.md","reason":"list scenarios and version cleanup"},{"path":".github/workflows/external-integration.yml","reason":"cleanup step also deletes run-scoped versions"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_external_integration_cloud_mutation_workflow.py","reason":"cover the version sweep in the cleanup step"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["relates_to","96b6-e89c-a78e-463e"],["relates_to","a15a-6936-2cee-479a"],["relates_to","af08-19c2-87b4-41d3"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"3dcd4fd6-843a-41c4-a61e-4f284e81d17d","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"7f23-e3dc-a2a6-457b","ticket_type":"story","title":"Live-test fix-version sync in the Jira Cloud mutation suite","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["6a4ef144-0138-496c-bfc0-d0012a10101b","6e17d122-5cf3-470c-9fa6-21605446c5b1","8717c6d2-a542-475e-ac05-56eb8834ee21","7325bd3b-50da-4a88-80d5-87e40e8e5158","a9dca208-a99f-4d8c-8f5b-455ef3897818","d481f05c-fe54-4270-8f8e-fc18ad2c488b","46da4982-8474-4476-af45-7366af27044f","32e4d76e-3a90-4006-8694-60b42884170d","e1fe8261-5f2e-462a-8bcc-660fd8e9b2d8","b229683a-c0e9-46e7-9b17-d61ed835b7df","3dcd4fd6-843a-41c4-a61e-4f284e81d17d","006975d0-ae9c-4b10-ba39-a496f61299c8","b0a0507f-63d0-48fa-895b-5c7324ad74b0"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794537233298101002,"uuid":"118ddfe6-5d7f-421a-9770-32bb63cdbbec"}